{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-pressure","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:quantum-pressure","kind":"definition","title":"Quantum pressure","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-temperature"],"tags":["pressure","statistical-mechanics","frobenius","boundary","q-anomaly"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.boundaryPressure","text":"quantum-pressure.md","leanSource":"quantum-pressure.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:quantum-pressure\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with quantum temperature <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_q = \\hbar_q</code>, let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U \\subset M</code> be a region of the brane with boundary <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\partial U</code> and <a href=\"#def:quantum-volume\" data-at=\"information-theory/stat-mech\">quantum volume</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_q</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{S}_q(K)</code> be the categorical action of a knot configuration <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U</code>. The <strong>quantum pressure</strong> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\partial U</code> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  P_q(U) = -\\,\\frac{\\partial F_q}{\\partial V_q}\\bigg|_{T_q},</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_q = -T_q \\ln Z_q</code> is the quantum free energy and</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  Z_q(U) = \\mathrm{tr}_{\\mathrm{Ad}} \\!\\sum_{K \\,\\in\\, \\mathrm{Conf}(U)} e^{-\\beta_q \\, \\mathfrak{S}_q(K)}</code></pre>\n<p>is the partition function over the configuration space <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Conf}(U)</code> of knot states in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta_q = 1/\\hbar_q = t_P(q)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-pressure.md","heading":"Definition","number":"22.9.6","page":"b/def-quantum-pressure","qa":{"counts":{"pass":83,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":68},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Information.boundaryPressure","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-pressure.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
